  "comments": [
    {
      "paragraph_index": 2,
      "comment": "Mix ingredients except sulfur, NaHCO3 and Na2S・9H2O, adjust pH to 6.5 and autoclave. Filter--sterilize 8% NaHCO3 solution and add to the medium. Steam sulfur for 3 hr on each of 3 successive days. Separately autoclave 5%Na2S・9H2O solution under a N2 atmosphere. Aseptically distribute the medium into culture vessels containing appropriate amount of sulfur (e.g., 20 mlculture medium in 120 ml serum bottle containing 0.24 g sulfur) under a H2--CO2 (4:1, v/v) gas mixture and seal with butyl rubber stoppers. Priorto inoculation, add the sterile Na2S・9H2O solution and readjust pH to 6.5, if necessary. Pressurize the inoculated bottles to 200 kPa H2--CO2 (4:1,v/v)."
    }
  ]
